# pyro_collisionshape

- Label: Pyro Collision Shape
- Category: Copernicus (`Cop`), Houdini 22.0.368
- Inputs: 0 to 1
- Parameters: 37 (exact, read from Houdini by hython)
- Used by the height graph: no

## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/pyro_collisionshape.html
- Summary (EN): Creates points that represent implicit surfaces, which add collision objects to a Pyro simulation. Mainly for basic primitives (box, sphere, torus, tube), and can also take a more complex implicit surface as its collision shape. Output is source_points, the points carrying Pyro collision attributes.
- Résumé (FR) : Pyro Collision Shape crée des points représentant des surfaces implicites (boîte, sphère, tore, tube) qui servent d'obstacles à une simulation Pyro.

- Inputs meaning: ["implicitsurface (optional): implicit surface built with the SOP-based implicit surface workflow"]

- Key parameters: ["Activation: 1 turns the node on, 0 turns it off", "Shape: selects the primitive, which determines the other controls", "Shape Box: Size (with per-component option), Roundness (0 gives sharp edges)", "Shape Sphere: Radius (with per-component option), Radius Scale, Cut Sphere with a Y-position plane", "Shape Torus: major and tube radius, Link Length (0 gives a regular torus)", "Shape Tube: Length, end Radius values (matching values give a straight tube), Radius Scale, Round Caps", "Transform: Translate, Rotate X Y Z, Uniform Scale", "Collision: Collision Velocity (motion-based velocity estimate for moving or rotating sources), Velocity Scale"]

- Caveats: ["Requires DOP-level permissions; not in Houdini Core, only in Houdini FX, Apprentice, Indie and Education", "Connect the output to the collision_points input of a Pyro Block Begin node", "For multiple collisions, merge several outputs with a Point Merge node", "The page does not describe the similarly named Pyro Collision from Shape node, which is only linked under See also"]

